# Noah: paths to skip. Gitignore syntax.
#
# The rule behind this list: we do not spellcheck code we did not write and do
# not intend to edit. Changing a comment in a vendored source would add noise to
# the diff against upstream, which is exactly what each PATCHES.md exists to
# keep small.

# Upstream sources, downloaded by bin/setup and never edited.
zsh-5.9/
awk-20260426/
bc-7.0.3/
ncurses-stub/
node_modules/

# Build trees, and the Emscripten loader, which is generated output.
build-zsh/
build-sed/
build-awk/
build-bc/
build-sbase/
build-diff/
web/zsh.js
npm/zsh.js

# Vendored C for the compiled builtins. Our own glue is re-included below —
# those files we did write, so they get checked.
sed-src/**
awk-src/**
bc-src/**
sbase-src/**
diff-src/**
!**/PATCHES.md
!**/LICENSE
!**/*_mod.c
!**/*_embed.c
!**/*_embed.h

# Verbatim license text. LICENSE reproduces the Zsh license word for word, and a
# legal notice is not ours to Americanize. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md is NOT here:
# its quoted texts sit in fenced blocks marked `noah:ignore` instead, so its own
# prose is still checked.
/LICENSE
npm/LICENSE
npm/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md

# The permit file necessarily contains the spellings it excuses.
/.noah/
